					<![CDATA[
						 <p>I personally think the defining factor of whether something is a joke SCP or not is if, on some level, you can take it seriously.</p> <p>For example, the fanfic plague is hilarious, but the idea of something like the Foundation losing extremely important records (and having no way to stop it) is srs business. Likewise, ROBO-DUDE is funny (see: ROBO-DANCE), but it messes with space (time?) and comes equipped with a rocket launcher and possibly a nuke, and it seems intended for children. And <em>that's</em> not funny.</p> <p>On the other hand, with the -J's, you have the likes of <span style="text-decoration: line-through;">Santa Claus</span> The Laplander, the Sun Launcher, and Darkblade.</p> 
				 	]]>
				</content:encoded>							</item>
